  <metadata>
    <id>tartube</id>
    <version>2.5.253</version>
    <title>Tartube</title>
    <authors>A. S. Lewis (and contributors)</authors>
    <owners>Adri</owners>
    <licenseUrl>https://tartube.sourceforge.io/#license</licenseUrl>
    <projectUrl>https://tartube.sourceforge.io/</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/axcore/tartube@master/icons/win/system_icon_256.png</iconUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>Tartube is a GUI front-end for youtube-dlc, youtube-dl and other compatible video downloaders.

It is partly based on youtube-dl-gui and is written in Python 3 / Gtk 3. Tartube runs on MS Windows, Linux, BSD and MacOS.

**32 bit users**: Due to an error (see issue: https://github.com/axcore/tartube#doesn-t-work-on-32-bit-windows), Tartube is no longer updated for the 32 bit version. if you need 32bit please install version: **2.3.332**

**Please Note**: This is an automatically updated package. If you find it is out of date by more than a day or two, please contact the maintainer(s) and let them know the package is no longer updating correctly.</description>
    <summary>A GUI front-end for youtube-dl, partly based on youtube-dl-gui and written in Python 3 / Gtk 3</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
# MAJOR NEW FEATURES
- Added new Traditional Chinese translation; thanks to arnolam
# MINOR NEW FEATURES
- Many users need to extract cookies from their browser, before downloading videos from YouTube. In Tartube, the settings for this have been moved out of the "Advanced download options" section; click Edit &gt; General download options &gt; Files &gt; Cookies to see them (Git #[793](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/793))
- You can now detach download options from a channel, playlist or folder (or even a video), without destroying the channel/playlist/folder itself (Git #[790](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/790))
- Changed the default Invidious server, since the old ones is defunct (Git #[796](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/796))
# MAJOR FIXES
- In the Videos tab, right-clicking a channel/playlist/folder inside another folder, and selecting Channel/Playlist/Folder actions &gt; Move to top level, produced a crash. Fixed it
- Fixed a crash when creating a video clip from another video clip (Git #[803](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/803))
- Added a workaround for an undiagnosed crash (Git #[798](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/798))
# MINOR FIXES
- Fixed python errors during video downloads (Git #[779](https://github.com/axcore/tartube/issues/779))
# 
**Full changelog:** [https://raw.githubusercontent.com/axcore/tartube/master/CHANGES](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/axcore/tartube/master/CHANGES)</releaseNotes>
